026,1817,26025,6078,2326,3039,448,1449,4462,315,279,30222,7263,11,323,3055,448,1817,4462,315,862,1828,2083,382,4340,1657,1424,927,2050,525,1052,304,2790,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nAt the national curling championships, there are three teams of four players each. After the championships are over, the very courteous participants each shake hands three times with every member of the opposing teams, and once with each member of their own team.\n\nHow many handshakes are there in total?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"47aca86e8d24e6ba46c66855df64feae12dbc8627d5feeca5888c9ec3945bcd3"},"seconds":32.53716826438904,"seed":147286131851350118,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we first identify the total number of players and the handshaking pattern among them.\n\n1. **Identify Total Number of Players:**\n   There are 3 teams, each consisting of 4 players.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of players} = 3 \\times 4 = 12\n   \\]\n\n2. **Handshakes Between Players of Different Teams:**\n   Each player shakes hands 3 times with each member of the other two teams.\n   - There are 2 other teams, each with 4 players.\n   - Thus, each player shakes hands \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) times with the members of the first opposing team and \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) times with the members of the second opposing team.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Handshakes per player with opposing teams} = 12 + 12 = 24\n   \\]\n   - Since there are 12 players in total, if we count the handshakes for each player, we initially get \\(12 \\times 24 = 288\\) handshakes. However, each handshake is counted twice (once for each participant), so we need to divide by 2.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total handshakes between different teams} = \\frac{288}{2} = 144\n   \\]\n\n3. **Handshakes Between Players of the Same Team:**\n   Each player shakes hands once with each member of their own team.\n   - There are 3 other members in the same team.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Handshakes per player with same team} = 3\n   \\]\n   - With 12 players in total, if we count the handshakes for each player, we get \\(12 \\times 3 = 36\\) handshakes. Again, each handshake is counted twice, so we divide by 2.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total handshakes within the same team} = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total Number of Handshakes:**\n   Adding the handshakes between different teams and within the same team gives:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total handshakes} = 144 + 18 = 162\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of handshakes is \\(\\boxed{162}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{162}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
